cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hull0k: 0 K convex hulls for binary alloys from LAMMPS potentials"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bitzek
    given-names: Erik
    affiliation: "Max-Planck-Institut für Nachhaltige Materialien (MPI for Sustainable Materials), Düsseldorf, Germany"
repository-code: "https://github.com/biterik/hull0k"
abstract: >-
  hull0k builds the 0 K formation-energy convex hull of a binary alloy system
  using an interatomic potential as the only energy engine. Every energy, force
  and minimisation is computed by a real LAMMPS binary running a real input
  script; Python only builds structures, orchestrates and analyses. For each
  candidate structure it reports the formation energy and the distance to the
  hull (e_above_hull) as the metastability measure, together with hull chemical
  potentials, vacancy and dilute substitution energies, and a comparison column
  of DFT formation energies from the Materials Project. It also computes the
  strained (epitaxial) hull under a biaxial in-plane constraint, in both the
  unstrained-reference and coherent-reference conventions, and reports every
  strain-induced change in hull membership.
keywords:
  - materials science
  - atomistic simulation
  - LAMMPS
  - convex hull
  - formation energy
  - phase stability
  - interatomic potentials
  - machine-learned potentials
  - epitaxy
  - special quasirandom structures
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
